# .bb-heavy.lock is STUCK — do not use it.
#
# Measured 2026-10-09 23:43: `flock -n` reports it HELD, but no process holds it in any
# namespace this sandbox can see (`fuser` finds none, the process table shows none) and the
# machine was idle (load 3.5 on 8 cores) when a lane blocked on it for 24 minutes. toml-lane
# lost two 10- and 30-minute guarded runs to it. It cannot be released by anyone who does not
# hold the descriptor, and it cannot be safely deleted while a real holder might exist.
#
# THE FLEET USES `.bb-heavy-v2.lock` INSTEAD. Update any command you have queued:
#     ( flock -w 600 9 || exit 9; <cmd> ) 9>.bb-heavy-v2.lock
#
# Before blaming the lock, check it is not simply busy: `flock -n 9 && echo FREE` 9>.bb-heavy-v2.lock
